    {
      "beat_id": "beat_006",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_002",
      "text": "Right now the Customers table is on screen, showing customer records rather than order data. This is the opposite table from where the extreme values we're looking for actually live.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 30,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_007",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_003",
      "text": "Click the Orders table entry in the list to select it.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 11,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_008",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_003",
      "text": "Right now the table appears in its original order, with rows listed as they were entered rather than arranged by the amount column. This order runs opposite to what would surface the extreme values at a glance.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 37,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_009",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_004",
      "text": "Click the Amount column header once to sort the table by that column.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_010",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_004",
      "text": "Right now the rows are arranged by order_date, with each entry following the last in date order rather than by dollar amount. That ordering runs opposite to what's needed for spotting the largest orders.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 34,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_011",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_005",
      "text": "Click the Amount column header once to sort the table by that column.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 13,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_012",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_005",
      "text": "Right now the Status column controls the sort order, with its values arranged in sequence across the rows. That direction doesn't reveal anything about which Amount values are largest or smallest.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 31,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_013",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_006",
      "text": "Let's click the Amount column header once to sort by it.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 11,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_014",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_006",
      "text": "Right now the Status column is arranged in ascending order, grouping rows alphabetically by their status label rather than by dollar value. That direction doesn't surface the largest amounts, since it's sorting text, not the Amount column.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 37,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_015",
      "attaches_to": "edge",
      "target_id": "edge_007",
      "text": "Click the Amount column header once to sort by it.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 10,
      "start_time": 0.0,
      "end_time": 0.0,
      "audio_path": null
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "beat_016",
      "attaches_to": "state",
      "target_id": "state_007",
      "text": "Right now the Status column is sorted, showing groupings by order status rather than by dollar amount. This arranges records in a direction unrelated to identifying the largest or smallest amounts.",
      "tts_text": null,
      "word_count": 31,
      "start_time": 0.0,
